__pycache__/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
uv.lock

# The synced quern package cache is COMMITTED, not ignored. quern.lock names its packages by
# digest, and ignoring the bytes those digests name meant CI had to fetch them from a registry
# — xag/quern-registry, which is frozen at ledger@0.4.1, so the check died on
# "craft@0.1.1 (pinned) is not in the library". The package is data; it travels with the lock.

# The publish runs record their nondeterminism boundary here; tapes are evidence, not source.
.quern/flight/

# The hooks record every judged turn here (craft.flight); same doctrine.
.craft/flight/

# Findings and the once-per-report markers: evidence about runs, not source. The
# seen-state advances on every turn of every session, so tracking it means a tree
# that is dirty whenever the hooks are alive.
.craft/seen.json
.craft/answers.jsonl
.craft/accounts-seen.json
.craft/residual-seen.json

# Convicted turns' false-positive reports, appended live by any session (craft.disputes);
# tracked state that every hook run dirties is state nobody can commit around.
.craft/disputes.jsonl
